      "text": "Chichicastenango Market and Lake Atitlán"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cc0efdab0d4ca3ba94d9abc38e00a07441dddc43cf93d7902dd4be9aa5a9aab6",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-f7d28995258f43d8b02d73d0103556dd",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, your driver will pick you up from your hotel at 07:30. The drive to Chichicastenango takes about 2.5 hours.\n\nHere you’ll visit one of the region’s most colourful traditional markets. The scent of incense, local customs and trading give the market its character. Bargaining is welcome when you shop. The market opens every Thursday and Sunday and carries on one of the Guatemalan Highlands’ oldest trading traditions.\n\nIn Chichicastenango, you can also see a church where Catholic practices coexist with Maya traditions.\n\nIn the afternoon, transfer to Lake Atitlán.\n\nOvernight at Porta Hotel del Lago in Panajachel."
    },
